enforcement|Ensuring compliance rather than merely publishing a rule is the boundary. Parking example is fictional, not a statement of current law; Vietnamese and enforcement of construction align.
imaginary|Non-real imagined entity is distinguished from creativity. Island example makes no unsupported geography claim, and Vietnamese tưởng tượng functions naturally as a modifier and standalone gloss.
primate|Biological boundary checked against Smithsonian primate classification including humans. Hands example avoids universal behavioural claims; religious title explicitly kept outside this draft meaning.
surprised|Experiencer adjective aligns with unexpectedly early library opening. Infinitive, clause and prepositional complements are sense-specific; no past-tense restriction derived from was surprised.
waste|Discarded substance, resource loss, transitive use and attributive adjective are separate supported ordinals. Vietnamese preserves materials, one hour and wrong folder; no artificial tense-based split.
